  "term": "meperidine",
  "definition": "Meperidine is a narcotic pain-relieving drug used for moderate to severe pain. In mental health contexts, it is relevant because prolonged use can cause morphine-type dependence, and withdrawal begins sooner than with morphine and tends to last a shorter time.",
